WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.067 --> 00:00:02.003
- It gives me so much hope and praise,

00:00:02.003 --> 00:00:04.026
just in life, to bring out blackness

00:00:04.026 --> 00:00:06.693
(sign swinging)

00:00:07.965 --> 00:00:09.187
- When it comes to Black History month

00:00:09.187 --> 00:00:10.873
I like to take a step back,

00:00:10.873 --> 00:00:14.041
go back to like the Africanism of it all.

00:00:14.041 --> 00:00:16.248
Got my little African
shirt on and whatnot.

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:17.731
Listen to a little bit of afrobeat,

00:00:17.731 --> 00:00:19.538
like make me feel
connected to the culture.

00:00:19.538 --> 00:00:22.097
- I celebrate resiliency,

00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:23.398
to persist through,

00:00:23.398 --> 00:00:25.819
and to be an example of
what our people fought for.

00:00:25.819 --> 00:00:27.932
- I'm inspired year round by black people.

00:00:27.932 --> 00:00:30.112
I love the extraness
that we kinda get during

00:00:30.112 --> 00:00:32.156
February that's not seen
the rest of the year.

00:00:32.156 --> 00:00:33.356
- I celebrate black culture

00:00:33.356 --> 00:00:35.358
and how universal it is

00:00:35.358 --> 00:00:37.899
and how similar it is
for all black people.

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:39.634
- Barack Obama, Michelle Obama.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:42.824
- The Obamas to really exemplify what joy

00:00:42.824 --> 00:00:44.705
and excellence looks like.

00:00:44.705 --> 00:00:46.777
- We are graced worldwide.

00:00:46.777 --> 00:00:49.244
Our culture, our music, our style.

00:00:49.244 --> 00:00:52.312
- It's about unity and loving one another.

00:00:52.312 --> 00:00:53.645
- I celebrate my father.

00:00:53.645 --> 00:00:57.900
Every February he would
have this deck of cards

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.817
of influential black
people throughout history.

00:01:03.304 --> 00:01:05.884
He would give us a card every day to read,

00:01:05.884 --> 00:01:09.907
and he's just tried all
his life to make sure

00:01:09.907 --> 00:01:11.707
that we know we're important,

00:01:11.707 --> 00:01:13.361
more than just our skin tone.

00:01:13.361 --> 00:01:15.230
- For my parents that
had to face adversity

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:19.265
and racism to raise two
half black and half white

00:01:19.265 --> 00:01:22.841
kids in the middle of
Arizona in the 1980s.

00:01:22.841 --> 00:01:25.419
- My parents who gave
me the life that I have.

00:01:25.419 --> 00:01:28.977
- My mom who although
is not African American

00:01:28.977 --> 00:01:32.361
has worked her ass off being there for us,

00:01:32.361 --> 00:01:35.429
trying to understand
the world that we see.

00:01:35.429 --> 00:01:38.924
- Me going natural now
is really from my mother

00:01:38.924 --> 00:01:41.951
and her whole outlook on
what it means to be natural

00:01:41.951 --> 00:01:45.149
and really just getting
back to the root of it all.

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:47.530
- Everyone who worked
tirelessly to give me everything

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.363
I have today.

00:01:48.363 --> 00:01:51.163
Rosa Parks, Martin Luther King, Malcolm X

00:01:51.163 --> 00:01:52.992
and all those guys that
kind of paved the way

00:01:52.992 --> 00:01:54.730
for all of black people.

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.818
- Sidney Poitier for
being the first black man

00:01:56.818 --> 00:01:57.874
to every win an Oscar.

00:01:57.874 --> 00:02:01.099
- I celebrate one of my favorite
activists, Maya Angelou.

00:02:01.099 --> 00:02:03.209
One of my favorite quotes is "I've learned

00:02:03.209 --> 00:02:05.119
"that people will for get what you said,

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:06.692
"people will forget what you did,

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:09.840
"but people will never forget
how you made them feel."

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.266
And that's something that I
try to carry with me every day.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:17.227
- I celebrate the music that
has come out of black history.

00:02:17.227 --> 00:02:19.686
- The Temptations, Aretha Franklin.

00:02:19.686 --> 00:02:21.698
- Miles Davis and Muddy Waters

00:02:21.698 --> 00:02:23.362
and guys that changed the game.

00:02:23.362 --> 00:02:25.813
- Sister Rosetta Tharpe, Billy Holiday,

00:02:25.813 --> 00:02:27.601
and Jimi Hendrix.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:28.668
- Bob Marley.

00:02:28.668 --> 00:02:31.034
I will say, in the year 2016.

00:02:31.034 --> 00:02:33.351
- You don't need an occasion
to celebrate Beyonce.

00:02:33.351 --> 00:02:34.927
You always celebrate Beyonce.

00:02:34.927 --> 00:02:35.882
- Jay-Z.

00:02:35.882 --> 00:02:36.735
- Solange.

00:02:36.735 --> 00:02:37.772
- Kendrick Lamar.

00:02:37.772 --> 00:02:39.417
- Change the Rapper was my shit.

00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:40.840
- Chance is an incredible artist,

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.343
an incredible father,

00:02:42.343 --> 00:02:44.973
ultimately one of the
leaders of our generation.

00:02:44.973 --> 00:02:47.727
- Spike Lee represents
for the black culture,

00:02:47.727 --> 00:02:50.055
does it in such a
beautiful way through film.

00:02:50.055 --> 00:02:52.269
- Moonlight. One of the
most incredible films

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:53.222
of our generation.

00:02:53.222 --> 00:02:55.752
I think the conversations
about what we believe

00:02:55.752 --> 00:02:58.170
blackness and black
masculinity to look like

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.197
was really important.

00:02:59.197 --> 00:03:01.482
Celebrating blackness in a way that's

00:03:01.482 --> 00:03:03.322
like really elevating the conversation.

00:03:03.322 --> 00:03:05.394
- We weren't pigeon-holed and
put into these little roles

00:03:05.394 --> 00:03:07.780
and just made to be side
characters or supporting cast.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.092
- And I really cannot like
leave out black women, you know.

00:03:11.092 --> 00:03:13.571
Black women and what
they've done for culture

00:03:13.571 --> 00:03:14.639
and what they're doing for us.

00:03:14.639 --> 00:03:17.289
- Finding strength and being
recognized for their beauty

00:03:17.289 --> 00:03:18.592
and their talent and their hard work.

00:03:18.592 --> 00:03:22.137
I'm inspired by women of
color who are taking strides

00:03:22.137 --> 00:03:24.899
behind the camera as
directors and producers,

00:03:24.899 --> 00:03:28.199
and also those women who
are in front of the camera

00:03:28.199 --> 00:03:31.676
and showing us this
dynamic and diverse world

00:03:31.676 --> 00:03:32.680
that we live in.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.704
- [All] That's what I celebrate.

00:03:34.704 --> 00:03:37.121
(calm music)

